# Line endings.
#
# Everything here runs on Linux: the container, the compose stack, CI, and the VPS
# this is meant to be deployed on. A CRLF in scripts/fork-core.sh becomes
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", and a CRLF in the Makefile breaks make —
# both of which are confusing failures that appear only for contributors on Windows.
#
# So the repository normalises to LF and checks out LF everywhere, regardless of a
# developer's core.autocrlf.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Files where a CRLF is not a style question but a broken file.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated or vendored: kept out of diffs and out of language statistics.
go.sum       -diff linguist-generated
docs/**      linguist-documentation
